621 - Gracious Father, Guard Thy Children
 / 
Key: A
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 621
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[A/E]Gracious Father, guard Thy children
[G#dim]From the foe's destructive power;
[Bm]Save, [A]O save [G#dim]them, [A]Lord, [F#m]from [A/E]falling
[A]In this dark and trying hour.
[G#dim]Thou [A]wilt [Bm]surely [A]prove Thy [E/B]people,
[G#dim]All our graces must be tried;
[A]But Thy [Bm]word illumes [A]our pathway,
[Bm]And in [A]God we still confide.

Verse 2:
[A/E]We are in the time of waiting;
[G#dim]Soon we shall behold our Lord,
[Bm]Wafted [A]far [G#dim]away [F#m]from [A/E]sorrow,
[A]To receive our rich reward.
[G#dim]Keep [A]us, [Bm]Lord, till [A]Thine appearing,
[G#dim]Pure, unspotted from the world;
[A]Let Thy [Bm]Holy [E/B]Spirit [A]cheer us
[Bm]Till Thy [A]banner is unfurled.

Verse 3:
[A/E]With what joyful exultation
[G#dim]Shall the saints Thy banner see,
[Bm]When [A]the Lord [G#dim]for [A]whom [F#m]we've [A/E]waited
[A]Shall proclaim the jubilee!
[G#dim]Freedom [Bm]from this [A]world's pollutions;
[G#dim]Freedom from all sin and pain;
[A]Freedom [Bm]from the [E/B]wiles [A]of Satan,
[Bm]And from [A]death's destructive [G#dim]reign.
